{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1537373648,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyMjg2NDExOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1860#issuecomment-422864119"},"message":"\u003e In V5 you can't unlock a file the content of which isn't present. Therefore it's now yielding an \"impossible\". This makes sense, since editing unknown content is obviously troublesome. In V6 however you can unlock a file without having its content and overwrite it with new content.\n\nIn my view, the fact that you can unlock a file without content in V6 is an implementation detail. You're still editing unknown content. If editing unknown content in V5 is troublesome, I don't see why it wouldn't be so in V6.\n\n\u003e What do we do if unlock is called on files without content in V6? We probably should indeed unlock, since that is what annex does.\n\nI think we should consider deviating from git-annex here. If a file's content isn't present, continue to report \"impossible\". This is consistent both from the UI perspective and conceptually.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1568977203,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzMzUwODE2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1860#issuecomment-533508167"},"message":"@kyleam 's conclusion is also the state of things in master. I am closing this issue, as there hasn't been a need to change that or discuss this topic for a year now.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1568977203,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjY0OTk0MTg0OA=="},"status":2}]}